{"module": "space-age", "key": "factoriopedia-description/fusion-generator", "en": "Consumes plasma from the [entity=fusion-reactor] to create electric energy. Power production is nominal, but less plasma is consumed if the temperature is higher. It outputs heated coolant equal to the amount of plasma consumed that can be cooled in an [entity=cryogenic-plant]. Fusion generators can be linked and transfer plasma to each other.", "hint": "", "reason": "missing"}
{"module": "space-age", "key": "factoriopedia-description/fusion-reactor", "en": "Uses fluoroketone coolant with fusion power cells to make super-heated plasma. It can only be output directly to an [entity=fusion-generator]. The neighbor bonus with other fusion reactors greatly increases the plasma temperature without increasing the amount of coolant used.", "hint": "", "reason": "missing"}
{"module": "space-age", "key": "fluid-description/fusion-plasma", "en": "Ultra-high-temperature ions generated in [entity=fusion-reactor] and consumed by a [entity=fusion-generator]. It is not a normal fluid and cannot be moved in [entity=pipe], it can only be moved through the Fusion reactor and Fusion generator.\\nThe temperature of plasma determines its energy value.\\nA quantity of plasma also represents that amount of coolant that travels with it, and the heated coolant is output by the Fusion generator as the plasma is used for energy.", "hint": "", "reason": "missing"}
